  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/8499856915baa0bf144561dd35143e024586f4d417ac4f9c1ee48d7586e0f26c.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=sin\u2061x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-sin\u2061x.$\n\n- Finally, translate it by $1$ unit **down** to give $y=-sin\u2061x-1.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-sin\u2061x-1.$",
